1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,440
You scan a QR code.

2
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:02,720
You type ten rupees.

3
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:03,740
You enter your PIN.

4
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:04,740
Beep.

5
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:05,720
Ten rupees received.

6
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:07,500
And you walk away with your chai, feeling

7
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:08,920
like a total tech genius.

8
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:09,820
Cute.

9
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:10,640
Here's the thing.

10
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,560
In those two seconds, two banks, a bunch

11
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,700
of computers, and one very serious referee

12
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,480
just held an emergency meeting.

13
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:17,960
About your chai.

14
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:19,920
So today, we're crashing that meeting.

15
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,420
Hi, I'm your host.

16
00:00:21,840 --> 00:00:23,440
And by the end of this video, you'll know

17
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:25,480
exactly where your ten rupees went.

18
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:27,780
And why, sometimes, it goes on a little

19
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:28,600
vacation.

20
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:33,193
First, meet the gang.

21
00:00:33,433 --> 00:00:35,513
There's you, holding a phone and a chai.

22
00:00:35,733 --> 00:00:37,493
There's your payment app, which, plot twist,

23
00:00:37,753 --> 00:00:39,153
does not actually keep your money.

24
00:00:39,453 --> 00:00:41,353
It's basically a very polite messenger.

25
00:00:41,913 --> 00:00:43,373
There's your bank, where your money actually

26
00:00:43,393 --> 00:00:44,133
lives.

27
00:00:44,153 --> 00:00:45,393
There's the chai wala's bank.

28
00:00:46,493 --> 00:00:48,753
And right in the middle, there's NPCI, the

29
00:00:48,773 --> 00:00:50,653
National Payments Corporation of India.

30
00:00:51,033 --> 00:00:51,993
Think of it as the referee.

31
00:00:52,653 --> 00:00:54,433
Nobody gets paid until the referee says

32
00:00:54,453 --> 00:00:55,093
so.

33
00:00:55,113 --> 00:00:56,913
Oh, and that QR code on the counter?

34
00:00:57,233 --> 00:00:59,713
It's just the chai wala's UPI ID, his name,

35
00:00:59,733 --> 00:01:01,633
and sometimes the amount, dressed up as

36
00:01:01,653 --> 00:01:02,453
a fancy square.

37
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:03,633
Very fashionable.

38
00:01:07,433 --> 00:01:09,073
Now, press pay, and watch closely.

39
00:01:09,613 --> 00:01:09,993
Step one.

40
00:01:10,013 --> 00:01:10,953
Your app writes a little message.

41
00:01:11,173 --> 00:01:12,593
Who's paying, who's getting paid, and how

42
00:01:12,613 --> 00:01:12,953
much.

43
00:01:12,973 --> 00:01:14,453
It hands it to its partner bank, which passes

44
00:01:14,473 --> 00:01:15,273
it to the referee.

45
00:01:15,413 --> 00:01:16,033
Step two.

46
00:01:16,053 --> 00:01:17,833
The referee looks at the chai wala's UPI

47
00:01:17,853 --> 00:01:19,673
ID and asks, which bank is this guy with?

48
00:01:19,693 --> 00:01:20,893
Like a phone book, but for money.

49
00:01:21,293 --> 00:01:21,873
Step three.

50
00:01:21,893 --> 00:01:23,273
The referee goes to your bank and says,

51
00:01:23,293 --> 00:01:25,013
this person wants to pay ten rupees.

52
00:01:25,193 --> 00:01:25,993
Is that okay?

53
00:01:26,393 --> 00:01:27,753
Your bank says, show me the PIN.

54
00:01:28,353 --> 00:01:28,913
Step four.

55
00:01:28,933 --> 00:01:30,713
Your bank checks the PIN, checks your balance,

56
00:01:30,853 --> 00:01:32,273
which, let's be honest, is always a tense

57
00:01:32,293 --> 00:01:33,753
moment, and takes out ten rupees.

58
00:01:34,293 --> 00:01:34,673
Step five.

59
00:01:34,693 --> 00:01:36,353
The referee tells the chai wala's bank,

60
00:01:36,373 --> 00:01:37,273
add ten rupees.

61
00:01:37,473 --> 00:01:38,053
Step six.

62
00:01:38,073 --> 00:01:39,173
Everyone sends everyone a confirmation,

63
00:01:39,193 --> 00:01:41,173
and the little speaker shouts, ten rupees

64
00:01:41,193 --> 00:01:41,873
received.

65
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:43,133
All of that, in about two seconds.

66
00:01:43,293 --> 00:01:44,733
Your chai hasn't even cooled down.

67
00:01:48,732 --> 00:01:50,012
Let's talk about your PIN.

68
00:01:50,672 --> 00:01:52,632
When you type it, your app can't actually

69
00:01:52,652 --> 00:01:53,352
read it.

70
00:01:53,372 --> 00:01:55,112
It's locked up right there on your phone,

71
00:01:55,132 --> 00:01:57,172
with a lock that only your bank can open.

72
00:01:57,312 --> 00:01:59,512
So the app is just carrying a sealed envelope

73
00:01:59,532 --> 00:02:00,952
it isn't allowed to peek into.

74
00:02:01,652 --> 00:02:02,452
Respect.

75
00:02:02,872 --> 00:02:04,712
And now, the most important thing in this

76
00:02:04,732 --> 00:02:05,532
entire video.

77
00:02:05,892 --> 00:02:07,752
You need your PIN to send money.

78
00:02:07,992 --> 00:02:09,852
You never, ever need it to receive money.

79
00:02:10,092 --> 00:02:12,632
So if a stranger says, enter your PIN to

80
00:02:12,652 --> 00:02:14,532
receive your prize, congratulations.

81
00:02:14,552 --> 00:02:17,492
The only prize is them, emptying your account.

82
00:02:21,498 --> 00:02:22,838
Now, the million rupee question.

83
00:02:23,298 --> 00:02:24,198
Who pays for all of this?

84
00:02:24,218 --> 00:02:25,958
When you swipe a card, the shop pays a small

85
00:02:25,978 --> 00:02:26,898
fee on every payment.

86
00:02:26,918 --> 00:02:28,878
But for regular UPI payments to shops?

87
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:29,738
The fee is zero.

88
00:02:29,918 --> 00:02:30,938
The government decided that.

89
00:02:31,098 --> 00:02:32,278
The banks were, let's say, not thrilled.

90
00:02:32,298 --> 00:02:33,798
So the government gives them some support

91
00:02:33,818 --> 00:02:34,738
to keep the lights on.

92
00:02:34,998 --> 00:02:36,518
Which means your ten rupee chai payment

93
00:02:36,538 --> 00:02:37,558
is low key sponsored.

94
00:02:37,938 --> 00:02:39,098
You're welcome, chai wala.

95
00:02:43,098 --> 00:02:45,238
And now, the scariest message in India.

96
00:02:45,838 --> 00:02:46,538
Money debited.

97
00:02:46,558 --> 00:02:47,358
Payment failed.

98
00:02:47,598 --> 00:02:48,398
What happened?

99
00:02:48,418 --> 00:02:50,258
Usually, your bank did take the money out,

100
00:02:50,398 --> 00:02:51,918
but somewhere after that, a confirmation

101
00:02:51,938 --> 00:02:52,858
got stuck.

102
00:02:53,278 --> 00:02:54,498
Maybe a server was slow.

103
00:02:54,778 --> 00:02:56,058
Maybe the network sneezed.

104
00:02:56,078 --> 00:02:57,918
So the system isn't sure the chai wala got

105
00:02:57,938 --> 00:02:58,478
paid.

106
00:02:58,498 --> 00:02:59,298
Don't panic.

107
00:02:59,898 --> 00:03:00,958
Your money isn't lost.

108
00:03:01,138 --> 00:03:02,258
It's just stuck in traffic.

109
00:03:02,698 --> 00:03:04,378
By the rules, it should come back to your

110
00:03:04,398 --> 00:03:06,358
account automatically by the next working

111
00:03:06,378 --> 00:03:07,018
day.

112
00:03:07,038 --> 00:03:08,758
And if the bank takes longer, the rules

113
00:03:08,778 --> 00:03:11,078
say it has to pay you a hundred rupees for

114
00:03:11,098 --> 00:03:12,018
every extra day.

115
00:03:12,038 --> 00:03:14,638
So technically, a slow bank could buy you

116
00:03:14,658 --> 00:03:15,458
ten chais.

117
00:03:19,264 --> 00:03:21,124
So, the next time you pay for chai, remember.

118
00:03:21,604 --> 00:03:23,204
An app, two banks, and a referee just had

119
00:03:23,224 --> 00:03:24,844
a two second meeting, all about you.

120
00:03:25,204 --> 00:03:26,904
Now multiply that by billions of payments,

121
00:03:26,924 --> 00:03:27,924
every single month.

122
00:03:28,084 --> 00:03:29,684
That's how a country of over a billion people

123
00:03:29,704 --> 00:03:30,604
buys its chai.

124
00:03:30,884 --> 00:03:32,224
Anyway, your chai's getting cold.

125
00:03:32,464 --> 00:03:33,144
Go drink it.

126
00:03:33,164 --> 00:03:34,484
And maybe tip the chai wala.

127
00:03:34,504 --> 00:03:35,924
Through UPI, obviously.
